[00:20:00Z] :: wifi4: radio-select 2/2 d11+0x03f6 pre=0x0001 wrote=0x0001 readback=0x0001 took=1 settle=1us — offset 0x01 is written UNADJUSTED: [SPEC-V3 RadioRegister] exempts it from the per-PHY-type address adjustment ("for all PHY versions, if the offset is 1, do not adjust the offset"), and no adjustment rule for PHY type 7 exists in either generation ::
[00:20:00Z] :: wifi4: RESTORE d11+0x03f6 <- pre-image 0x0000 readback=0x0000 restored=MATCH — compared against the RECORDED pre-image, never against 0x0001 ::
[00:20:00Z] :: wifi4: radio-id raw=0x0205917f order=V4(lo-then-hi) hi=0x0205 lo=0x917f rev=0 ver=0x2059 mfg=0x17f expected-mfg=0x17f MATCH — field layout [SPEC-V3 RadioID] + [SPEC-V4 802.11/Radio/RadioID], both generations agreeing: rev=bits31:28, ver=bits27:12, mfg=bits11:0 ::
[00:20:00Z] :: wifi4: radio-id cross-check v3-agree=0 (V3 order hi-then-lo=0x0000917f vs V4 order lo-then-hi=0x0205917f — the two spec generations state OPPOSITE read orders for this one 32-bit register and neither says whether a data port latches on read, so both are executed; agreement means the value is not an artefact of our sequencing) addr-echo=1 (0x3F6 read back 0x0001 and 0x0001, want 0x0001 — a MISMATCH means the running PSM moved the shared latch between our write and our read and the word above is not ours to decode) dark=0 ::
[00:20:00Z] :: wifi4: radio-id verdict=VALID gated-on=mfg-is-0x17F+addr-echo+not-dark order=V4 — those three are the WHOLE gate, on the V4-order word; the V3 order is the printed alternative (f13-f20: hi=0, the latch shape), not a term. The radio VERSION is deliberately NOT in it ::
[00:20:00Z] :: wifi4: radio-ver 0x2059 vs 0x2059 MATCH (ADVISORY, [TREE], NOT GATED — bcm4331.md §S5's "2059" is this repository's own prose. Neither generation's radio-version table carries 0x2059 or any HT-PHY radio ([SPEC-V3 RadioID]: 0x2050/0x2051/0x2053/0x2055/0x2060; [SPEC-V4 802.11/Radio/RadioID]: 0x2050/0x2051/0x2055/0x2060/0x2062), so gating on it would be gating on a guess. Same discipline as §S4-W5 residual 4 for the ucode revision number: print what the silicon publishes, gate only on what is cited) ::
[00:20:00Z] :: wifi4: phy-alive raw=0x9701 analog=9 type=7 expected=7 rev=1 ioctl=0x00002055 phy-reset=0 want=0 resetctl=0x00000000 want=0 macctl=0x80020402 psm-run=1 want=1 verdict=PHY-ALIVE — [SPEC-V4 802.11/PHY]'s PHY-type table pins 7 = HT PHY (Three Stream N) from a Group-A source, which is the first non-b43-lineage corroboration this tree has for EXPECT_PHY_TYPE. Read-back predicate for §S5(b): a PHY that still decodes to type 7, with the core out of reset and the PSM running, on the far side of a reset that destroyed the resident image ::
